  "headline": "MPR Reviews Mahfud MD Concerns Over Vice President Election Date",
  "seoTitle": "MPR Discusses Vice President Election Date",
  "metaDescription": "The MPR is reviewing legal concerns raised by Mahfud MD regarding the scheduled December 9 vice presidential election to replace Gibran.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The MPR has scheduled the inauguration of a new vice president for December 9, 2026, to replace Gibran.",
    "Mahfud MD cautioned that the selection process could be legally invalid if it does not adhere to specific mandatory timelines.",
    "The MPR ad hoc committee is currently reviewing the concerns raised while proceeding with candidate verification preparations."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has scheduled the election and inauguration of a new vice president for December 9, 2026. This process follows the vacancy left by Gibran. President Prabowo is required to submit two candidates for the position by November 25. However, legal concerns have emerged regarding the timeline for the selection process. Mahfud MD has publicly argued that the December 9 date could render the election legally void, suggesting that a 14-day working period should be observed after the submission of names to prevent political complications. In response, members of the MPR ad hoc committee stated that they are reviewing these notes while continuing their work on candidate verification and drafting the necessary decrees for the selection and inauguration procedures. Three working groups have been established to handle the verification of 22 specific candidate requirements.",
